{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/29610","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:35.485497+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"NONE","body":"I have tested that putting\n```python\nmain_fn.trace(jax.random.PRNGKey(0)).lower()\n```\nbefore\n```python\nout = rehydrated_fn.call(jax.random.PRNGKey(0))\n```\nmakes the seg-fault go away.\nSo it seems that lowering `main_fn` in the process creates something needed to make the exported function call work.  \nBut I am not familiar with the JAX compilation internals and why that could be the case.","created_at":"2025-06-22T15:29:00Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/29610#issuecomment-2994277052","id":2994277052,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/29610","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc6yeQq8","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2994277052/reactions"},"updated_at":"2025-06-22T15:29:00Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2994277052","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40721229?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/markus7800","id":40721229,"login":"markus7800","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzIxMjI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"NONE","body":"Has anyone an idea for this bug. I intend to use JAX for a research project and have to rely on the export functionality.","created_at":"2025-07-01T17:09:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/29610#issuecomment-3024876112","id":3024876112,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/29610","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc60S_JQ","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/3024876112/reactions"},"updated_at":"2025-07-01T17:09:20Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/3024876112","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40721229?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/markus7800","id":40721229,"login":"markus7800","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzIxMjI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"NONE","body":"After some digging I found that `jax.lax.linalg.cholesky` is the culprit.\n\nAfter exporting like\n```python\nimport jax.export\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\nchol = jax.jit(jax.lax.linalg.cholesky)\ninput = jnp.eye(1)\nexported_main = jax.export.export(chol)(input)\nwith open(\"tmp.bin\", \"wb\") as file:\n    file.write(exported_main.serialize())\n```\nimporting (in a new process) causes a segmentation fault (on CPU)\n```python\nwith open(\"tmp.bin\", \"rb\") as file:\n    exported_fn = bytearray(file.read())\n    rehydrated_fn = jax.export.deserialize(exported_fn)\n    out = rehydrated_fn.call(input)  # seg-fault\n    print(out)\n```\nAdding `chol.trace(input).lower()` before importing makes the segfault go away.\nAgain, this bug occurs only in my CPU installation and not in my CUDA JAX installation.","created_at":"2025-07-17T06:23:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/29610#issuecomment-3082737099","id":3082737099,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/29610","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc63vtXL","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/3082737099/reactions"},"updated_at":"2025-07-18T13:35:01Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/3082737099","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40721229?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/markus7800","id":40721229,"login":"markus7800","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzIxMjI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus7800","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"### Description\n\nHello,\n\nI am trying to call an exported JAX function.\nUnfortunately, on my CPU jax installations it only seems to work when I have exported the function in the same Python process, otherwise I get a segmentation fault.\nI have tested this on two machines (M2 Pro, Linux).\nThis only seems to affect the CPU jax installations, as everything works as expected on my Linux cuda installation.\n\nI have included a script to reproduce the bug below.\n\nRun following steps:\n1. `python3 test_advi_export.py -export` works on all machines\n2. `python3 test_advi_export.py` **run after step 1.** causes seg-fault on CPU installation, works on CUDA installation\n\nBest,\nMarkus\n\nUPDATE: I managed to reduce the minmal reproducible example, see comments.\n\n### System info (python version, jaxlib version, accelerator, etc.)\n\nMacbook M2 Pro CPU jax installation\n```\njax:    0.6.2\njaxlib: 0.6.2\nnumpy:  2.2.2\npython: 3.13.5 (main, Jun 11 2025, 15:36:57) [Clang 17.0.0 (clang-1700.0.13.3)]\ndevice info: cpu-1, 1 local devices\"\nprocess_count: 1\nplatform: uname_result(system='Darwin', node='Markuss-MacBook-Pro-14.local', release='24.2.0', version='Darwin Kernel Version 24.2.0: Fri Dec  6 18:56:34 PST 2024; root:xnu-11215.61.5~2/RELEASE_ARM64_T6020', machine='arm64')\n```\n\nDesktop Ryzen 5950x CPU jax installation\n```\nWARNING:2025-06-20 16:04:50,510:jax._src.xla_bridge:794: An NVIDIA GPU may be present on this machine, but a CUDA-enabled jaxlib is not installed. Falling back to cpu.\njax:    0.6.2\njaxlib: 0.6.2\nnumpy:  2.3.0\npython: 3.13.1 (main, Dec  9 2024, 00:00:00) [GCC 14.2.1 20240912 (Red Hat 14.2.1-3)]\ndevice info: cpu-1, 1 local devices\"\nprocess_count: 1\nplatform: uname_result(system='Linux', node='fedora', release='6.12.10-200.fc41.x86_64', version='#1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri Jan 17 18:05:24 UTC 2025', machine='x86_64')\n```\nDesktop GPU cuda jax installation\n```\njax:    0.6.2\njaxlib: 0.6.2\nnumpy:  2.2.4\npython: 3.13.1 (main, Dec  9 2024, 00:00:00) [GCC 14.2.1 20240912 (Red Hat 14.2.1-3)]\ndevice info: NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1070-1, 1 local devices\"\nprocess_count: 1\nplatform: uname_result(system='Linux', node='fedora', release='6.12.10-200.fc41.x86_64', version='#1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri Jan 17 18:05:24 UTC 2025', machine='x86_64')\n\n$ nvidia-smi\nFri Jun 20 16:08:04 2025       \n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| NVIDIA-SMI 565.77                 Driver Version: 565.77         CUDA Version: 12.7     |\n|-----------------------------------------+------------------------+----------------------+\n| GPU  Name                 Persistence-M | Bus-Id          Disp.A | Volatile Uncorr. ECC |\n| Fan  Temp   Perf          Pwr:Usage/Cap |           Memory-Usage | GPU-Util  Compute M. |\n|                                         |                        |               MIG M. |\n|=========================================+========================+======================|\n|   0  NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1070        Off |   00000000:2B:00.0  On |                  N/A |\n|  0%   48C    P2             50W /  180W |     434MiB /   8192MiB |      2%      Default |\n|                                         |                        |                  N/A |\n+-----------------------------------------+------------------------+----------------------+\n                                                                                         \n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| Processes:                                                    